 concept_h: 'Reveal rather than show', concept_p: 'We do not show a photo of the wall. Visitors discover each trace themselves, as with a torch. We remember better what we discover ourselves.',
 c1_h: 'Light up', c1_p: 'With your finger or mouse, the light reveals the messages on the wall.',
 c2_h: 'Understand', c2_p: 'Each message has a record: its story, an audio version and a truth label.',
 c3_h: 'Pass on', c3_p: 'Families add memories. A historian checks them before anything is published.',
 who_h: 'For whom?', w1_h: 'Pupils', w1_p: 'In class, they discover a real trace and tell its story.', w2_h: 'Visitors', w2_p: 'At the memorial, on their phone, in their language: French, English, Spanish or Arabic.', w3_h: 'Families and historians', w3_p: 'Families share, historians check. Memory grows without losing accuracy.',
 labels_h: 'A truth label on every record', labels_p: 'You always know where information comes from and whether it has been checked. We do not hide what we do not know.',
